  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "Session 1 (researcher-10): drafted full proof of the complex polarization identity in Mathlib's sesquilinear-in-first-argument convention. Documented the convention mismatch with the textbook physics formula (the slug's stated formula computes ⟪y,x⟫ = conj⟪x,y⟫ in Mathlib, not ⟪x,y⟫). 12 theorems organized into 7 sections: norm expansion helpers, real-part recovery, imaginary-part recovery via I-shift, per-component recovery formulas, main theorem (Mathlib convention), physics-convention bridge, algebraic corollaries. Build pending.",
    "builtItems": [
      "norm_add_sq_complex: ‖x+y‖² = ‖x‖² + 2 re⟪x,y⟫ + ‖y‖² (restate Mathlib for ℂ)",
      "norm_sub_sq_complex: ‖x-y‖² = ‖x‖² - 2 re⟪x,y⟫ + ‖y‖² (derive via inner_neg_right)",
      "norm_add_sq_sub_norm_sub_sq_eq_four_re: ‖x+y‖² - ‖x-y‖² = 4 re⟪x,y⟫_ℂ",
      "norm_smul_I_sq: ‖I•y‖² = ‖y‖²",
      "re_I_mul: re(I*z) = -im(z)",
      "norm_add_smul_I_sq_sub_eq_neg_four_im: ‖x+I•y‖² - ‖x-I•y‖² = -4 im⟪x,y⟫_ℂ (sign flipped from physics)",
      "re_inner_eq_quarter_norm_diff: re⟪x,y⟫_ℂ = (‖x+y‖² - ‖x-y‖²)/4",
      "im_inner_eq_quarter_norm_diff: im⟪x,y⟫_ℂ = (‖x-iy‖² - ‖x+iy‖²)/4 (sign flip)",
      "complex_polarization_mathlib (MAIN): ⟪x,y⟫_ℂ = (‖x+y‖² - ‖x-y‖² + i(‖x-iy‖² - ‖x+iy‖²))/4",
      "physics_polarization_eq_inner_swap: physics formula = ⟪y,x⟫_ℂ",
      "physics_polarization_eq_conj: physics formula = conj⟪x,y⟫_ℂ",
      "mathlib_minus_physics: ⟪x,y⟫_ℂ - ⟪y,x⟫_ℂ = 2i · im⟪x,y⟫_ℂ"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "**Convention mismatch is real**: slug's stated formula is physics convention. In Mathlib (math convention), the same formula computes ⟪y,x⟫ = conj⟪x,y⟫, not ⟪x,y⟫. Stating the identity correctly requires choosing — and documenting — a convention.",
      "**Sign flip on imaginary correction**: with Mathlib's ⟪c•x, y⟫ = conj(c)·⟪x,y⟫, replacing y with iy gives ⟪x, iy⟫ = i·⟪x,y⟫, whose real part is -im⟪x,y⟫. So ‖x+iy‖² - ‖x-iy‖² = -4 im⟪x,y⟫ — opposite sign from physics convention.",
      "**Decomposition via Complex.re_add_im is the cleanest proof**: rather than Complex.ext + arithmetic, write z = re(z) + im(z)·i and substitute the per-component formulas, leaving only push_cast; ring to finish.",
      "**inner_conj_symm is the bridge**: in Mathlib, swapping arguments and conjugating are the same operation, so the physics formula recovers the swapped inner product."
    ],
